# The recipe CSVs are the frozen evaluation protocol. Git must not rewrite a byte of
# them: core.autocrlf=true on Windows converts CRLF -> LF on commit, which changes the
# file's hash without changing its content, and makes the integrity check in notebook 01
# report a mismatch that is not one. The csv module writes CRLF on every platform, so
# -text keeps the committed bytes identical to what Kaggle produces.
data/recipes_*.csv -text
